OEKG:30ef233f-8c93-2c2c-bf46-8bc7168b12e3 a OEO:OEO_00020227 ;
    RDFS:label "Langfristszenarien fuer die Transformation des Energiesystems in Deutschland 3"^^XSD:string ;
    OBO:BFO_0000051 <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/publication/5a3ffdae-06fb-fb0a-fd42-dfb7517d9e2a>,
        <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/scenario/15304c1e-3ac2-3a3d-7b85-b282ccb5aa06>,
        <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/scenario/7f1e3589-2523-9d18-5db4-2aa5c9a77410>,
        <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/scenario/bbdae7dc-6959-a348-1f61-0251d4016bec> ;
    DC:abstract "The project \"Long-term scenarios for the transformation of the energy system in Germany\" examines the techno-economic effects of alternative paths to decarbonizing the energy system and how Germany can achieve the goal of greenhouse gas neutrality. Specifically, three scenarios are summarized in this report. Decarbonization requires climate-neutral energy sources. Essentially, these are electricity, hydrogen and/or synthetic hydrocarbons. For this first report, we have modeled a scenario with very high use of each energy source (TN-Electricity, TN-H2-G, TN-PtG/PtL)."^^XSD:string ;
    DC:acronym "LFS-3"^^XSD:string ;
    OEO:OEO_00000510 OEKG:6af34013-ba78-181a-fd22-9b00087c6c2d,
        OEKG:6b9c4f04-e7f9-4bc6-b433-bd7e54583b78,
