OEKG:7cbe1492-4173-85b9-685a-356b0228ecbc a OEO:OEO_00020227 ;
    RDFS:label "Zukunftslabor Energie"^^XSD:string ;
    OBO:BFO_0000051 <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/frameworks/167>,
        <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/frameworks/258>,
        <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/models/312>,
        <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/publication/04acb907-ee9d-3beb-4c88-10ac81f41bc8>,
        <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/publication/3671a8e1-795b-1b28-cea3-1f9c653ce155>,
        <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/publication/5df9173d-2f6b-59d4-4bf7-4c50a1fd82fa>,
        <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/publication/83c83e54-b5cf-1eed-cc24-b7d3c960c27e>,
        <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/publication/8dcd8110-4ede-18d2-b664-caa3ae0b9847>,
        <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/publication/b519261c-100b-7722-c90b-71abb5bdea6d>,
        <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/publication/c04ebbcb-12a2-e43d-8b35-828785b54d34>,
        <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/scenario/8c659939-c4c4-b11d-8bbc-0f1549a3c549>,
        <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/scenario/98b1c446-f586-e159-7dca-6de310777f7a>,
        <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/scenario/cb3c50f6-4c59-4948-0781-98e96beb5b5e>,
        <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/scenario/fa1532b9-fb42-bb8a-9c10-1ae7e6e033a0> ;
    DC:abstract """Digitalization plays an important role in energy systems and for the energy transition. It supports or enables the recording, monitoring, communication, analysis and optimization of measured values as well as the (remote) control of decentralized energy conversion plants and equipment for more efficient operational management, which adapts to the highly dynamic, changing processes of the energy industry in a largely automated manner. An energy system that integrates several sectors such as electricity, gas or heat creates flexibility on the one hand in order to be able to react to the forecasting uncertainty of decentralized, supply-dependent energy feed-in. At the same time, it drastically increases system complexity - with implications for modeling and control. In addition to an understanding of new interaction dynamics in an integrated energy and information system, completely new approaches are required to analyze and optimize this cyber-physical energy system-of-systems.

Central aspects of the Future Energy Laboratory are machine learning and big data analytics in energy systems, cyber-resilient energy systems and information security, information and communication technology-based integration of new players in the system and deployment planning of decentralized energy systems as well as interoperability and standardized processes of multimodal energy systems."""^^XSD:string ;
    DC:acronym "ZLE"^^XSD:string ;
    OEO:OEO_00000509 OEKG:3a8affce-e71f-6caf-d893-31e2777944a9 ;
    OEO:OEO_00000510 OEKG:1c0e07b0-c0be-1124-5ae5-ee0e95d74c07,
        OEKG:2a502e63-60e4-cdfb-a53d-e9b62b1c2a39,
