OEKG:b5e3f952-889c-0154-36e2-b8546d9d9390 a OEO:OEO_00020227 ;
    RDFS:label "dena-Leitstudie Aufbruch Klimaneutralitaet - Eine gesamtgesellschaftliche Aufgabe"^^XSD:string ;
    OBO:BFO_0000051 <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/publication/3af15d41-603c-4cf0-7228-5336be660908>,
        <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/scenario/438ce4e0-1755-9819-2529-8e126b6e3e14>,
        <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/scenario/4c00a319-483e-8814-4eb0-d39a57c956c6>,
        <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/scenario/9e8d1bdf-8711-ee4f-4321-ae4326699820>,
        <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/scenario/eca4d6bb-1bbb-ddf5-8c60-ccdddf7f7e3e>,
        <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/scenario/fe123931-9d68-636f-b9b0-8438b5dd0139> ;
    DC:abstract """The final report of the dena flagship study Aufbruch Klimaneutralitt identifies key areas of action and solutions for achieving climate neutrality in Germany by 2045. More than ten scientific institutes and a 45-member advisory board with high-ranking experts from science, politics and society have contributed their expertise. Over 70 companies contributed their industry experience and market assessments in discussions. Findings from various expert reports and discussions have been incorporated into this final report.

The dena flagship study offers specific solutions and CO2 reduction pathways for the buildings, transport, industry, energy, agriculture and LULUCF sectors. Variants are analysed in four pathways in order to achieve the model scenario of climate neutrality by 2045. In addition to a comprehensive and differentiated analysis, a total of 84 tasks were identified in ten central fields of action, which are intended to provide guidelines for the coming legislative period."""^^XSD:string ;
    DC:acronym "dena-2045"^^XSD:string ;
    OEO:OEO_00000510 OEKG:96ca1cf8-2783-ef34-3838-c859fe8f1f03 ;
