<https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/scenario/897456cd-35f8-329a-fd0c-2e38c2ae6cc1> a OEO:OEO_00000365 ;
    RDFS:label "Directed Transition"^^XSD:string ;
    DC:abstract "Carbon-mitigating energy technologies emerge and require strong policy incentives for their uptake and development. The storyline assumes that the effect of grassroots and citizen-led initiatives will be minimal but that strong policy incentives can drive the required engagement of citizens to reach climate targets. This storyline is driven by a strong centralized vision on the part of policymakers and direct partnerships with industry and technology developers who respond to incentives provided by the public sector and provide broad advances in low-carbon energy-related technologies."^^XSD:string ;
    DC:acronym "Hainsch-Directed"^^XSD:string ;
