<https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/scenario/fa1532b9-fb42-bb8a-9c10-1ae7e6e033a0> a OEO:OEO_00000365 ;
    RDFS:label "DSZ Grid Operation"^^XSD:string ;
    DC:abstract "The scenario investigates the possibilities of coupled laboratory infrastructures for flexibilizing low-voltage electrical grids as a scalable platform in energy research. The objective is to test the platform in responding to grid instabilities, such as voltage drops, and evaluate the performance of different components, including battery storage systems and heat pumps, in providing flexibility to the grid. Using a combination of real-time simulators, virtual machines, and communication gateways to connect three geographically separated laboratories enables the users to utilize laboratory hardware of different energy sectors."^^XSD:string ;
    DC:acronym "DSZ-grid"^^XSD:string ;
    OEO:OEO_00020222 <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/https://www.omg.org/spec/LCC/Countries/ISO3166-1-CountryCodes/Germany> ;
    OEO:OEO_00390073 OEO:OEO_00020411,
        OEO:OEO_00030010 ;
    OEO:OEO_00390095 "fa1532b9-fb42-bb8a-9c10-1ae7e6e033a0"^^XSD:string .

<https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oekg/scenario/fc576787-3173-181a-370c-41b91ea74d56> a OEO:OEO_00000365 ;
    RDFS:label "MIX"^^XSD:string ;
    DC:abstract "Relying on both carbon price signal extension to road transport and buildings and strong intensification of energy and transport policies. With its uniform carbon price, it reflects either an extended and fully integrated EU ETS or an existing EU ETS and a new ETS established for road transport and buildings with emission caps set in line with cost-effective contributions of the respective sectors. Maritime transport sector is assumed to be included in the existing EU ETS in MIX."^^XSD:string ;
    DC:acronym "EU-Core-MIX"^^XSD:string ;
